{"id": "EUVD-2026-107890", "enisaUuid": "321d082f-d258-3005-9e1e-e77128e83896", "description": "Traefik before v2.11.58 and v3.7.14 contains an authentication bypass vulnerability in its SNI check, which is skipped when request TLS state is nil. Unauthenticated clients can send HTTP/2 requests with the :scheme http pseudo-header over TLS on Go 1.27 builds to reach routers requiring client certificates without presenting one.", "datePublished": "2026-10-22T01:43:36", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T01:43:36", "baseScore": 7.0, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:N/SC:H/SI:H/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/traefik/traefik/security/advisories/GHSA-fh26-gfpp-7xxx", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/traefik-before-2.11.58-and-3.7.14-sni-check-bypass-via-http-2-scheme"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-114635", "GHSA-m6hw-6pp7-2ffc"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "b837dfb3-97cf-3075-b0bb-9b47bef75779", "product": {"name": "traefik", "vendor": {"name": "traefik"}}, "product_version": "3.0.0 <3.7.14"}, {"id": "cdd35716-3cf5-3e09-8e7f-1c5c1ed02995", "product": {"name": "traefik", "vendor": {"name": "traefik"}}, "product_version": "0 <2.11.58"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "76b35bee-4d4a-3972-afd5-c81c50035745", "vendor": {"name": "traefik"}}], "isExploited": false}